added_lemmas.statement:
For \(c^\dagger=(1,-1/4,-3/4)\), restriction of nature to schedules satisfying \(y_{i,2}=y_{i,3}\) for every unit gives exactly the unrestricted two-treatment binary game.  Consequently,
\[
 \begin{aligned}
 R_n(c^\dagger)
 &\ge
 \inf_{\mathcal D_n,\widehat\tau}
 \max_{\substack{y\in\{0,1\}^{n\times3}\\
                  y_{i,2}=y_{i,3}\ (1\le i\le n)}}
 \mathbb E_{\mathcal D_n}\!\left[
 \{\widehat\tau-\tau_{c^\dagger}(y)\}^2\right]\\
 &=\rho_n^\star
 =\frac1n-C_A n^{-4/3}+o(n^{-4/3}).
 \end{aligned}
\tag{TA}
\]
Moreover \(C_A>\Lambda_{c^\dagger}=C_A(5/8)^{2/3}\), so \((\mathrm{TA})\) is strictly weaker at second order than the sharp three-arm lower bound.
